-----BEGIN COSIGN-PLACEHOLDER-----
# OP-763 D2 — cosign verification material.
#
# OmniSight signs published images with **cosign keyless**
# (sigstore / fulcio / rekor) — see `.github/workflows/build-images.yml`.
# Keyless verification does NOT require a static public key; the
# signature carries a short-lived certificate whose identity claims
# (workflow ref + OIDC issuer) are what `verify_image_signature.sh`
# checks by default.
#
# This file exists for two future cases:
#
#   1. Air-gapped / offline-mirror environments where the verifier
#      cannot reach rekor.sigstore.dev or fulcio.sigstore.dev. Drop
#      a long-lived ed25519 key generated with `cosign generate-key-pair`
#      here, sign with `cosign sign --key cosign.key`, and the
#      verifier picks up the key automatically when
#      `--cosign-pub deploy/cosign/cosign.pub` is passed (or when
#      this file's contents are non-placeholder).
#
#   2. Migration off sigstore. If sigstore is ever deprecated as the
#      project's signing backbone, replace this file with the new
#      project key and update the Spec section in
#      `docs/operations/release-image-pipeline.md`.
#
# The placeholder header (`-----BEGIN COSIGN-PLACEHOLDER-----`) is
# load-bearing: `verify_image_signature.sh` checks for it and falls
# back to keyless verification when the file is still a placeholder.
# Replace the entire file contents with a real
# `-----BEGIN PUBLIC KEY-----` block to switch to key-based mode.
-----END COSIGN-PLACEHOLDER-----
